 "title": "PLL clock multiplier, 14 MHz to 200 MHz, 3.3 V or 5.0 V",
 "source": {
  "document": "NB3N511/D",
  "revision": "Rev. 5, January 2019",
  "pages": 8
 },
 "summary": "A phase-locked-loop clock multiplier in SOIC-8 that takes a fundamental-mode crystal of 5 to 32 MHz, or a reference clock of 1 to 50 MHz, and puts out a TTL/CMOS clock of up to 200 MHz at nine selectable multiples of that input, from 2X to 8X. Two select pins with three levels each (tied low, tied high or left open) choose the multiple. Pulling OE low puts the output in high impedance. It runs from 3.3 V ±10% or 5.0 V ±5% over -40 °C to +85 °C and is offered as a lower-cost stand-in for a crystal oscillator.",
 "key_figures": [
