 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Clock path",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A crystal oscillator, or the clock on X1/ICLK, feeds a divide-by-P stage into a phase detector, charge pump and VCO; the VCO output goes back through a divide-by-M feedback divider. S1 and S0 set the multiplier, and the VCO drives a TTL/CMOS output stage on CLKOUT gated by OE. The multiplication carries zero ppm error."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Multiplier select",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "S1 and S0 each read three levels: tied to GND (L), tied to VDD (H) or left open (M, held at VDD/2 inside). The nine combinations give 2X, 2.5X, 3X, 3.333X, 4X, 5X, 5.333X, 6X or 8X. The input frequency times the multiplier has to fall between 4 and 200 MHz. They may be tied to the VDD and GND pins or to the planes."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Example",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "With a 20 MHz fundamental crystal and S1 = L, S0 = H (5X), CLKOUT runs at 100 MHz."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output enable",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "OE has an internal pull-up of 270 kΩ, so the output runs when OE is open. Driving OE low tri-states CLKOUT; enable and disable each take 50 ns typical."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Decoupling",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "A 0.01 µF capacitor goes from VDD (pin 2) to GND (pin 3), placed close to the package to keep lead inductance low."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Crystal and its capacitors",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Use a fundamental-mode, parallel-resonant crystal; third-overtone crystals are not to be used. About 12 pF of capacitance sits on the chip. Lay out pads for a small capacitor from X1 to ground and another from X2 to ground; they add to the board stray capacitance to reach the crystal's nominal load. Since trimming can only add capacitance, keep the traces between crystal and chip very short and free of vias. Each capacitor is (CL - 12 pF) × 2."
  },
  {
   "topic": "External reference clock",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "A reference clock of 1 to 50 MHz drives X1/ICLK, with X2 left unconnected. Its input thresholds sit about VDD/2: high at (VDD/2) + 1 V and low at (VDD/2) - 1 V at 5 V, ±0.7 V at 3.3 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Series termination",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "For a clock trace longer than one inch, a 33 Ω series resistor can sit next to the CLKOUT pin. The output's nominal impedance is 20 Ω."
  }
 ],
